cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the archived release and the paper."
title: "Detecting unknown arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi from linked long-read rRNA gene sequences: code and data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "O'Brien"
    given-names: "Aaron"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ayobi/amf-novelty-benchmark"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23219690"
version: "0.3.2"
date-released: "2026-11-01"
abstract: >-
  Code, curated culture reference and benchmark outputs for naming long-read AMF rRNA gene sequences by
  MaarjAM virtual taxon, UNITE species hypothesis and LSU species clade, and for detecting species absent
  from the reference. Release 0.3.2 adds the per-round outputs of the LSU-removal test (36 species rounds
  with their own placement and 15 genus rounds) and analyses of the ITS distance rule's robustness; it leaves
  out the manuscript text until the preprint is posted. Release 0.3.1 added the results of the EUKARYOME
  test; release 0.3.0 added the controls of the SSU-discordance flag, the complex rule within each round, the
  resampled intervals and the evidence per class of divergent sequence. Tables and other outputs are
  CC BY 4.0 (DATA_LICENSE.md).
keywords:
  - arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi
  - rRNA genes
  - long reads
  - metabarcoding
  - novelty detection
